Security Update Policy for Chromium Embedded Framework
========================================================

CEF Release Cycle
-----------------

CEF follows the Chromium release cycle. When Chromium releases a new
version, CEF is updated to match.

Chromium Security Updates
--------------------------

Chromium security updates are released frequently, often multiple times
per month for critical vulnerabilities.

Maintainer Commitment
---------------------

The maintainer commits to:

  1. Monitoring security.debian.org/tracker/chromium for security updates
  2. Monitoring https://chromereleases.googleblog.com/ for Chrome releases
  3. Rebuilding CEF within 7 days of Chromium security releases
  4. Coordinating with Debian Chromium team when possible

Testing/Unstable Only
---------------------

Due to the frequency of Chromium security updates and the significant
build time required (2+ hours, 40GB disk space), this package is
targeted for unstable/testing only.

Stable releases would require dedicated security team support, which
is not currently available.

Per-Package Security ACLs
--------------------------

Bug #817285 (per-package security ACLs) has been IMPLEMENTED as of
September 2023. This infrastructure allows packages like CEF to be
maintained in unstable/testing without blocking other packages.

Migration to chromium-source
-----------------------------

When bug #893448 (chromium-source package) is implemented, CEF security
updates will flow automatically from the Debian Chromium team's work.
This will significantly reduce the maintenance burden.

Until then, CEF will be rebuilt whenever Chromium is updated in Debian.

Reporting Security Issues
--------------------------

Security issues in CEF should be reported to:

  1. Upstream CEF: https://bitbucket.org/chromiumembedded/cef/issues
  2. Debian maintainer: vejeta@gmail.com
  3. Debian Security Team: team@security.debian.org

Scope
-----

This security policy applies to:

  - libcef137: The CEF shared library
  - libcef-dev: Development files
  - cef-resources: Resource files

All three packages are updated together when CEF is rebuilt.

